From b09ab97f4b77c9f2d8f7a06d0154654eb82d807e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:21:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add [ocean] air_sea_fluxes = "core": Large & Yeager
 (NCAR/CORE) bulk formulae over open water
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With [sea_ice] air_ice_fluxes = "core" (138), the whole surface follows NEMO's CORE
bulk formulae (GLORYS12) and the OMIP-2 protocol for JRA55-do. The default stays
"similarity" (NumericalEarth's Monin–Obukhov fluxes with a constant Charnock 0.02).
Adds a smoke config, a 30-day twin of 138's stress run, and CORE versions of the
two hindcast configs (new experiment names).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Abhhvox5x2icdiKzZoAA2j
